Denis Razuvaev created KAFKA-14890:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Kafka initiates shutdown due to connectivity problem =
with Zookeeper and FatalExitError from ChangeNotificationProcessorThread
                 Key: KAFKA-14890
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-14890
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
    Affects Versions: 3.3.2
            Reporter: Denis Razuvaev


Hello,=20

We have faced several times the deadlock in Kafka, the similar issue is - h=
ttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-13544=20

The question - is it expected behavior that Kafka decided to shut down due =
to connectivity problems with Zookeeper? Seems like it is related to the in=
ability to read data from */feature* Zk node and the _ZooKeeperClientExpire=
dException_ thrown from _ZooKeeperClient_ class. This exception is thrown a=
nd it is caught only in catch block of _doWork()_ method in {_}ChangeNotifi=
cationProcessorThread{_}, and it leads to {_}FatalExitError{_}.=20

This problem with shutdown is reproduced in the new versions of Kafka (whic=
h already have fix regarding deadlock from 13544).=C2=A0
It is hard to write a synthetic test to reproduce problem, but it can be re=
produced locally via debug mode with the following steps:=20
1) Start Zookeeper and start Kafka in debug mode.=20
2) Emulate connectivity problem between Kafka and Zookeeper, for example co=
nnection can be closed via Netcrusher library.=20
3) Put a breakpoint in _updateLatestOrThrow()_ method in _FeatureCacheUpdat=
er_ class, before _zkClient.getDataAndVersion(featureZkNodePath)_ line exec=
ution.=20
4) Restore connection between Kafka and Zookeeper after session expiration.=
 Kafka execution should be stopped on the breakpoint.
5) Resume execution until Kafka starts to execute line _zooKeeperClient.han=
dleRequests(remainingRequests)_ in _retryRequestsUntilConnected_ method in =
_KafkaZkClient_ class.=20
6) Again emulate connectivity problem between Kafka and Zookeeper and wait =
until session will be expired.=20
7) Restore connection between Kafka and Zookeeper.=20
8) Kafka begins shutdown process, due to:=20
_ERROR [feature-zk-node-event-process-thread]: Failed to process feature ZK=
 node change event. The broker will eventually exit. (kafka.server.Finalize=
dFeatureChangeListener$ChangeNotificationProcessorThread)_=20

The following problems on the real environment can be caused by some networ=
k problems and periodic disconnection and connection to the Zookeeper in a =
short time period.=C2=A0

I started mail thread in [https://lists.apache.org/thread/gbk4scwd8g7mg2tfs=
okzj5tjgrjrb9dw] regarding this problem, but have no answers.

For me it seems like defect, because Kafka initiates shutdown after restori=
ng connection between Kafka and Zookeeper, and should be fixed.=C2=A0

Thank you.



