When running the command _kafka-streams-application-reset --bootstrap-serve=
rs $BOOTSTRAP --application-id foo_=C2=A0all changelog and repartition topi=
cs that=C2=A0_starts with_ foo is deleted. This happens even if there's no =
application-id named foo.

Example:
{code:java}
Application IDs:
foo-v1
foo-v2

Internal topics:
foo-v1-repartition-topic-repartition
foo-v2-repartition-topic-repartition=20

Application reset:
kafka-streams-application-reset --bootstrap-servers $BOOTSTRAP --applicatio=
n-id foo
> No input or intermediate topics specified. Skipping seek.
Deleting inferred internal topics [foo-v2-repartition-topic-repartition, fo=
o-v1-repartition-topic-repartition]
Done.{code}
Expected behaviour is that the command fails as there are no application-id=
's with the name foo instead of deleting all foo* topics.=C2=A0

