Thank you for the continuous work, I have some small problems related to =
the implementation details:

1. We have decided to add a new metadata.version, and you have said that =
 "We should also avoid gating on metadata.version to include the =
`OnlineLogDirectories` field in the broker registration, the existing =
versioning in the message schemas should suffice to guarantee =
compatibility",  I think this is a big difference from what we had done =
in the past design, it's better to add this point in  "Compatibility, =
Deprecation, and Migration Plan " section.
2. Related to (1),  an important thing about migration is that we should =
first upgrade controllers before upgrade brokers since broker will only =
send `BrokerRegisterationRequest` once and we should use the new format =
and the controller should recoganize the new format, this is difficult =
in co-resident mode, so you should point out that we only support =
distributed mode similar to KIP-866.
3. What will happen on receiving "AssignReplicasToDirsRequest"? this =
should be described in "Controller" section, for example, generating =
`PartitionChangeRecord` or return error code.

Apart from these problems, this KIP LGTM,=20
--
Best,
Ziming


> On Sep 28, 2022, at 04:59, Igor Soarez <i@soarez.me> wrote:
>=20
> Hi Ziming,
>=20
> Thank you for having another look at this KIP, and please accept my =
apologies as to my delay in replying.
>=20
> The migration introduces JBOD support, so before the migration there =
should only be one log directory configured per broker. This assumption =
simplifies how the controller learns about the initial log directory =
placement for existing partitions. The first broker registration =
referencing log directories must declare a single log directory - which =
must be online as brokers cannot start without any online log dirs. If =
there are no previous log dirs registered for this  broker, the =
controller assigns all existing partitions in the broker to this single =
directory.
>=20
> Since we assume a single log dir per broker as a migration starting =
point and brokers cannot start without any online log directories, the =
`OfflineLogDirectories` field simply cannot be used in the first =
registration after the upgrade. However, the issue you described applies =
to `OnlineLogDirectories`. If use of this field is gated by =
metadata.version then we do require a double roll for brokers to make =
their first registration with a log directory.
>=20
> As you describe, we could move the list of online log directories from =
the broker registration request to the heartbea request, but I believe =
we shouldn't do this because:
>  a) The intention is to address a transient problem =E2=80=94 the =
migration into the feature, which should happen only once =E2=80=94 by =
accepting a long term commitment as to how the online log dirs are =
signaled.
>  b) While the log directory status can change at any point from online =
to offline, the list of existing log directories is static for broker's =
lifetime, so it makes little sense to send this information over and =
over again to the controller.
>=20
> We should also avoid gating on metadata.version to include the =
`OnlineLogDirectories` field in the broker registration. If the =
controllers are upgraded first, the existing versioning in the message =
schemas should suffice to guarantee compatibility. After the controllers =
are upgraded, the brokers can then be upgraded and each of them can =
register their single online log directory from the first instantiation.
>=20
> Please, let me know if this makes sense and any other thoughts you =
might have.
>=20
> Best,
>=20
> --
> Igor
>=20
> On Thu, Sep 1, 2022, at 2:04 AM, deng ziming wrote:
>> Hi Igor,
>>=20
>> I think this KIP can solve the current problems, I have some problems=20=

>> relating to the migration section.
>>=20
>> Since we have bumped broker RPC version and metadata record version,=20=

>> there will be some problems between brokers/controllers of different=20=

>> versions. In ZK mode we use IBP as a flag to help solve this, in =
KRaft=20
>> mode we use a feature flag(metadata.version) as a flag for using new=20=

>> RPC/metadata or not.=20
>>=20
>> Assuming that we are upgrading from 3.3 to 3.4, firstly the finalized=20=

>> version of metadata.version is 3.3, brokers will use version 1 of=20
>> `BrokerRegistrationRequest` which contains no =
`OfflineLogDirectories`,=20
>> finally the finalized version of metadata.version is 3.4, but brokers=20=

>> will no longer send `BrokerRegistrationRequest` unless we restart the=20=

>> broker, so controllers can=E2=80=99t be aware of the =
`OfflineLogDirectories` of=20
>> each broker, so we should reconsider the suggestion of Jason to use=20=

>> `BrokerHeartbeatRequest` to communicate `OfflineLogDirectories`.
>>=20
>> Of course this problem can be solved through a double roll(restart=20
>> broker twice when upgrading), but we should trying to avoid it since =
we=20
>> now have feature flag.
>>=20
>> One solution is that we include `OfflineLogDirectories` both in=20
>> `BrokerRegistrationRequest` and `BrokerHeartbeatRequest` requests, =
when=20
>> upgrading from 3.3 to 3.4 the=20
>> `BrokerRegistrationRequest.OfflineLogDirectories` is empty whereas =
when=20
>> upgrading from 3.4 to 3.5 it will not be empty. And maybe we can also=20=

>> remove `LogDirectoriesOfflineRequest` you proposed in this KIP.
>>=20
>> --
>> Best,
>> Ziming
>>=20
>>=20
>>> On Aug 18, 2022, at 11:24 PM, Igor Soarez <i@soarez.me> wrote:
>>>=20
>>> Hi Ziming,
>>>=20
>>> I'm sorry it took me a while to reply.
>>>=20
>>> Thank you for having a look at this KIP and providing feedback.
>>>=20
>>>> 1. We have a version field in meta.properties, currently it=E2=80=99s=
 1, and we can
>>>> set it to 2 in this KIP, and we can give an example of =
server.properties and
>>>> it=E2=80=99s corresponding meta.properties generated by the storage =
command tool.
>>>=20
>>>> 2. When using storage format tool we should specify cluster-id, it =
will be an
>>>> arduous work if we should manually specify directory-ids for all =
log dirs,
>>>> I think you can make it more clear about this change that the =
directory-ids
>>>> are generated automatically.
>>>=20
>>> Thank you for these suggestions. I've updated the KIP to:
>>>=20
>>> * include an example
>>> * clarify that the version field would be changed to 2
>>> * clarify that the log directory UUIDs are automatically generated
>>>=20
>>>> 3. When controller place a replica, it will select a broker as well =
as a log
>>>> directory, the latter is currently accomplished in the broker side, =
so this
>>>> will be a big change?
>>>=20
>>> I think there can be benefits, as Jason described previously, if we =
change how
>>> log directories are assigned as follow-up work.
>>>=20
>>> =46rom a codebase surface area perspective, it is definitely a big =
change
>>> because there are many models, types and interfaces that assume =
replicas are
>>> identified solely by a broker id.
>>> That will have to change to include the directory UUID, many lines =
of code will
>>> be affected.
>>>=20
>>> But in terms of behavior it shouldn't be a big change at all. =
Brokers currently
>>> select the log directory with the least logs in it. This isn't a =
very nice
>>> policy, as logs can have wildly different sizes, and log directories =
can have
>>> different capacities. But it is a policy that the controller can =
keep.
>>>=20
>>> If we decide to extend the selection policy and keep it in the =
broker,
>>> the broker will continue to be able to override the controller's =
selection
>>> of log directory, using the `AssignReplicasToDirectories` RPC.
>>>=20
>>>> 4. When handling log directory failures we will update Leader and =
ISR using
>>>> the existing replica state machine, what is this state machine =
referring to,
>>>> do you mean the AlterPartition RPC?
>>>=20
>>> No, I mean that it will use the same rules and mechanism
>>> (`PartitionChangeBuilder`) that is used when a broker is fenced, =
shutdown or
>>> unregistered.
>>>=20
>>> I think maybe the term "replica state machine" isn't the very =
appropriate.
>>> I've updated the KIP to rephrase this section.
>>>=20
>>> Thanks,
>>>=20
>>> --
>>> Igor


